        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">In a stage-gate process, a Gateway closes one ProductDevelopmentStage and opens another, given that certain conditions are met.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Input -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Input">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Input"/>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <owl:Class>
                                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                                    <owl:Class>
                                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                                            <owl:Restriction>
                                                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#hasArtefact"/>
                                                <owl:minQualifiedCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:minQualifiedCardinality>
                                                <owl:onClass rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Artefact"/>
                                            </owl:Restriction>
                                            <owl:Restriction>
                                                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#hasComponent"/>
                                                <owl:minQualifiedCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:minQualifiedCardinality>
                                                <owl:onClass rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Component"/>
                                            </owl:Restriction>
                                            <owl:Restriction>
                                                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#hasParameter"/>
                                                <owl:minQualifiedCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:minQualifiedCardinality>
                                                <owl:onClass rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Parameter"/>
                                            </owl:Restriction>
                                        </owl:unionOf>
                                    </owl:Class>
                                    <owl:Restriction>
                                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#inputInto"/>
                                        <owl:minQualifiedCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:minQualifiedCardinality>
                                        <owl:onClass>
                                            <owl:Class>
                                                <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                                                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#DevelopmentActivity"/>
                                                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#TemporalConstruct"/>
                                                </owl:unionOf>
                                            </owl:Class>
                                        </owl:onClass>
                                    </owl:Restriction>
                                </owl:intersectionOf>
                            </owl:Class>
                            <owl:Restriction>
                                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#hasEnvironment"/>
                                <owl:minQualifiedCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:minQualifiedCardinality>
                                <owl:onClass rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Environment"/>
                            </owl:Restriction>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Output"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#TemporalConstruct"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An Input consists of the things that are necessary in order to begin a particular DevelopmentActivity or TemporalConstruct in the development process.

For example, a Twin is an Artefact. Supposing we have a Twin as the Output from one DevelopmentActivity. In order to continue developing the Twin during the next DevelopmentActivity, it will have to be passed in as part of the Input to that DevelopmentActivity.

An item of information, such as a Datapoint, may also form part of the Input. For example, we may need to track the weight in kg of a Component through the development process. This would be done using the same Datapoint included into the Input into a DevelopmentActivity, which then becomes part of the Output from that same activity.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Iteration -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Iteration">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Iteration"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#hasDevelopmentActivity"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#DevelopmentActivity"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#duringTemporalPartition"/>
                        <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#TemporalPartition"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#isRepeated"/>
                        <owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:hasValue>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#TimeStructure"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Span"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/helenoliver/ontologies/2026/2/figure8secondattempt#Step"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An Iteration groups DevelopmentActivities that are carried out together in Cycles that may be repeated. 

Iterations that share characteristics in frequently recurring patterns during the development process have been defined as subclasses. These subclasses are not exhaustive.

Unless otherwise stated, the DevelopmentActivities in an Iteration are assumed to be taking place in parallel.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


